  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring equitable participation of all IOC Member States in IOC programmes and activities by assistance in capacity development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CD: Implementation of the 2030 Agenda will require equitable participation by all MS in IOC activities.The IOC Capacity development strategy (2023-2030) defines 6 essential outputs. Through 2024-2025 the CD strategy will be implemented by global and regional IOC programmes and aligned with the CD chapter (challenge 9) of the UN Decade. IOC CD will further focus on matching CD opportunities provided by Member States and CD demand from Member States through the Ocean CD-Hub. Gender: statistics of applicants and students/lecturers participating in courses will be maintained. The GOSR will continue gathering information on strategic investments in ocean science and to identify gaps in capacity that need to be addressed to fully realize SDG 14.</narrative>
  </description>
